import json
from pathlib import Path
r=Path(__file__).parent
lessons=json.loads((r/'content.json').read_text())
extra=[
('Turn a specification into a test oracle','Separate input validity from output validity. For two-sum, multiple correct pairs may exist, so comparing one exact pair with a reference can reject a valid solution. Instead validate indices, distinctness, and sum; if no pair is returned, check that the baseline finds none.','Input [1,4,2,3], target 5 has pairs (0,1) and (2,3). An output validator accepts either. A single expected-output array is an incomplete oracle.'),
('Prove the merge, then the recursion','During merge, the output prefix contains the smallest consumed elements in sorted order. Each step preserves that claim by choosing the smaller remaining front. Strong induction handles the recursion: singleton ranges are sorted, recursive halves are sorted by hypothesis, and the merge preserves both order and multiset.','For half-open ranges [lo,hi), mid=lo+(hi−lo)/2. The calls [lo,mid) and [mid,hi) cover every item once. The condition hi−lo≤1 handles empty ranges as well.'),
('Reason about dependent loops','Nested syntax alone does not imply quadratic cost. Count the total executions of the innermost operation, accounting for changing bounds. For a two-pointer scan whose pointers never retreat, each pointer moves at most n times, so the total may be linear.','If j starts at 0 outside the outer loop and only increases while j<n, the inner body executes at most n times across the entire run. Resetting j=0 inside each iteration changes that bound.'),
('Why bottom-up heap construction is linear','Most nodes are close to leaves and can move only a short distance. At most about n/2^(h+1) nodes have height h. Summing their O(h) work gives O(n·Σh/2^h)=O(n). This differs from inserting n items individually, which can cost O(n log n).','In a complete heap of 15 items, 8 leaves need no sift, 4 parents move at most 1 level, 2 move at most 2 levels, and the root at most 3. Bound work by 4+4+3 rather than 15×3.'),
('Deletion is part of the search invariant','In linear probing, lookup stops at a never-used slot. A deleted slot cannot become never-used while later collided keys still depend on probing through it. Use tombstones and continue searches across them; periodically rebuild if tombstones accumulate.','Keys hashing to 2 occupy slots 2,3,4. Delete slot 3. Searching for the key in slot 4 must continue past the tombstone. An empty slot 3 would incorrectly terminate the search.'),
('Exchange arguments justify greedy choices','Take a lightest edge e crossing a cut that respects the current forest. If an MST does not contain e, adding it creates a cycle. That cycle has another cut-crossing edge f with weight at least e. Replacing f with e preserves a spanning tree without increasing weight.','The proof guarantees a lightest crossing edge belongs to some MST. With tied weights it need not belong to every MST. This is why a different valid selection order can still be correct.'),
('A shortest-path trace needs unreachable states','Initialize all distances to infinity and only the source to zero. Before relaxing u→v, check that u is reachable; adding a weight to an infinity sentinel can overflow and invent a path. A DAG permits negative edges, because each dependency is processed once in topological order.','If source 0 reaches 1, but vertex 2 is unreachable from the source with an edge 2→3(−10), vertices 2 and 3 remain unreachable. Do not compute INF−10 and treat it as a real improvement.'),
('Reconstruct a solution without changing the objective','A numerical optimum is not a witness. In edit distance, backtrack from (n,m): an equal diagonal needs no edit, a paid diagonal substitutes, a step to (i−1,j) deletes, and a step to (i,j−1) inserts. Resolve ties consistently and reverse the collected operations.','For a→ab, the optimum is 1. Backtracking first removes the trailing insertion transition, then matches a. If rolling rows save memory, reconstruction needs stored decisions or a more advanced divide-and-conquer method.'),
('Use one hash convention consistently','With high-order leading symbols, prefix[i+1]=(prefix[i]·p+symbol[i]) mod M and hash(l,r)=prefix[r]−prefix[l]·p^(r−l) mod M. Both formulas use half-open intervals. Java remainder may be negative, so normalize. Comparing different lengths also requires checking their lengths.','For symbols 1,2,3 and base 10, prefix=[0,1,12,123]. The substring [1,3) is 123−1×100=23. This convention avoids modular inverses for substring queries.'),
('Build failure links in breadth-first order','Aho–Corasick failure links must refer to states whose shorter-prefix information is already available. Initialize root children with failure=root. For each transition v→u by c, follow failure[v] until a c transition exists or the root is reached. Store output links to terminal suffixes to avoid copying large output lists.','For she, the state she has failure he when he is a trie prefix. Reporting only she misses he at the same ending position. Output links recover suffix matches with work proportional to reported occurrences.')]
for l,(t,b,e) in zip(lessons,extra):
 if not any(s['title']==t for s in l['sections']):l['sections'].append(dict(title=t,body=b,example=e))
 l['objectives']=[f'Explain {x.lower()} using a concrete input.' for x in l['topics']]+['State an invariant and justify the time and space bounds.']
 l['recall']='Without looking back, explain why the algorithm works, name one assumption it needs, and construct an input that breaks a tempting alternative.'
(r/'content.json').write_text(json.dumps(lessons,indent=2,ensure_ascii=False))
q=json.loads((r/'questions.json').read_text());q=[x for x in q if not x.get('expanded')]
def add(l,p,options,a,why,skill):q.append(dict(id=len(q),lesson=l,prompt=p,options=options.split('|') if options else None,answer=a,type='mc' if options else 'input',why=why,skill=skill,expanded=True))
data=[
(1,'An algorithm returns indices (2,2) for [5,1,3] and target 6. Which contract condition fails?','Both indices are within bounds|Both selected values sum to target|The selected indices are distinct|The input values must be sorted',2,'Using one index twice violates the distinct-index requirement, even though 3+3=6.','Contracts'),
(1,'A correct two-sum implementation returns a different valid pair from your oracle. What should your checker do?','Reject unless both arrays are identical|Validate the returned pair against the contract|Accept only the lexicographically first pair|Sort the returned values and compare lengths',1,'When several outputs are valid, check the specification rather than one canonical output.','Validation'),
(2,'Merge Sort on an empty half-open range [k,k) should:','Return without reading the array|Read a[k] to create a singleton|Split into two ranges of length one|Merge with the next nonempty range',0,'The base case hi−lo≤1 includes length zero and prevents invalid reads.','Boundaries'),
(2,'T(n)=4T(n/2)+n. What is the tight asymptotic bound?','Θ(n log n)|Θ(n²)|Θ(n² log n)|Θ(n³)',1,'n^(log₂4)=n² dominates the linear combine work.','Recurrences'),
(3,'A pointer j is initialized once and increases at most n times across n outer iterations. The inner-body total is:','Θ(n²) in every case|O(n) across the run|Θ(log n) across the run|O(1) across the run',1,'Count total pointer moves, not just the syntactic loop nesting.','Operation counting'),
(3,'Which result would establish a tight Θ(g(n)) bound on the same cost function?','An O(g(n)) proof alone|An Ω(g(n)) proof alone|Both O(g(n)) and Ω(g(n)) proofs|Two measured runtimes proportional to g(n)',2,'A tight asymptotic bound needs both eventual upper and lower bounds.','Bounds'),
(4,'A binary min-heap is [1,4,2,7,5]. Remove its root. Which array can result after standard sift-down?','[2,4,5,7]|[4,2,5,7]|[2,7,4,5]|[5,4,2,7]',0,'Replace 1 with 5, then swap with the smaller child 2. The remaining heap is [2,4,5,7].','Heap trace'),
(4,'Why does bottom-up heap construction improve over repeated insertion?','It sorts all nodes before the first sift|Most nodes have small height and little sift work|It avoids comparing parent and child keys|All nodes are already in heap order',1,'The height-weighted sum of sift work is linear.','Heap analysis'),
(5,'Linear probing stores collided keys in slots 2,3,4. Slot 3 is deleted. Which action preserves lookup?','Mark 3 never-used and stop searches there|Mark 3 deleted and keep probing across it|Move slot 4 to an arbitrary empty slot|Remove every key with the same hash',1,'Tombstones preserve probe chains. A never-used marker would hide keys beyond it.','Deletion'),
(5,'A trie stores “team” and “tea”. How many non-root nodes are needed?',None,'4','The shared path t→e→a has three nodes; m adds one. Both a and m are terminal.','Trie trace'),
(6,'Two equal-weight edges cross a cut. The cut property guarantees that each lightest edge:','Appears in every MST|Can appear in some MST|Must be excluded by Kruskal|Connects a unique pair of components',1,'The exchange argument gives existence in some MST; equal weights may allow alternatives.','Greedy proof'),
(6,'Perform union(0,1), union(1,2), union(3,4), union(2,4) on 6 singleton sets. How many sets remain?',None,'2','Four successful unions reduce six components to two: {0,1,2,3,4} and {5}.','DSU trace'),
(7,'An isolated vertex has no incoming or outgoing edges. In an SCC decomposition it:','Belongs to no component|Forms a singleton component|Joins the source component|Makes decomposition undefined',1,'Reachability includes a zero-length path from a vertex to itself.','SCC definitions'),
(7,'Why guard dist[u] != INF before relaxing a DAG edge u→v?','To ensure all edge weights are positive|To prevent sentinel arithmetic inventing a reachable path|To keep the topological order lexicographic|To ensure every vertex has an outgoing edge',1,'Only reachable prefixes can extend real paths; INF arithmetic may overflow or become spuriously smaller.','Shortest paths'),
(8,'What is the unit-cost edit distance between the empty string and “abcd”?',None,'4','Insert all four characters. This is the D[0][j]=j base case.','DP base cases'),
(8,'LCS(“abc”,“ac”) has length:',None,'2','The subsequence ac uses positions 0 and 2; contiguity is not required.','Subsequences'),
(9,'With high-order hash H(abc)=123 and base 10, what is H(bc) without modulus effects?',None,'23','Subtract leading contribution 1×100.','Hash convention'),
(9,'Pattern “aaaa” has final prefix-function value:',None,'3','Its longest proper prefix that is also a suffix is aaa.','Prefix function'),
(10,'For suffix array [2,1,0] of “aaa”, what is LCP[2] under the previous-suffix convention?',None,'2','Compare suffixes aa and aaa: common prefix aa has length two.','Kasai trace'),
(10,'Aho–Corasick with patterns “a” and “aa” scans “aaa”. How many matches should be reported?',None,'5','Three a matches and two aa matches; overlapping occurrences count.','Output links')]
for x in data:add(*x)
for item in q:
 if 'skill' not in item:item['skill']=lessons[item['lesson']-1]['topics'][0]
(r/'questions.json').write_text(json.dumps(q,indent=2,ensure_ascii=False))
